            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0005\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F048:F050\", \"F053\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Under clause (ii) (F048:F050) and clause (iii) (F053), the parent and the local educational agency consenting in writing to excusal and the member submitting written input prior to the meeting are two distinct statutory requirements. The member's written input does not satisfy or replace the separate requirement of written parental consent.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0004\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F053\", \"F056\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Subparagraph (D) (F056) requires that an invitation to the initial IEP meeting be sent to the subchapter III representative 'at the request of the parent.' The statute does not condition this invitation on written parental consent, nor does clause (iii) (F053) apply outside clauses (i) and (ii).\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0003\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F048:F050\", \"F053\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Clause (iii) (F053) explicitly establishes that a parent's consent under clause (ii) (F048:F050) shall be in writing. Adding this context quote and qualifying condition to C0005 accurately reflects the statutory conditions governing IEP Team member excusal.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F046\", \"F053\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Clause (iii) (F053) explicitly provides that a parent's agreement under clause (i) (F046) shall be in writing. Incorporating this context quote and condition into C0004 accurately reflects the statutory requirements governing attendance excusal when an area is not being modified or discussed.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F032:F043\", \"F053\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Subparagraph (B) (F032:F043) defines the composition of the IEP Team, and clause (iii) (F053) applies only to parental agreement and consent under clauses (i) and (ii) of subparagraph (C). The source contains no requirement that every team member's participation requires prior written parental consent.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F046\", \"F053\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Clause (iii) (F053) mandates only that a 'parent’s agreement under clause (i) and consent under clause (ii) shall be in writing.' It does not mandate that the local educational agency's agreement under clause (i) be in writing.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
